From a1a1a92e8e8d060a20cf6e22ad3a47a411191873 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:25:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 081/274] TileLang V4.1 MoE: one rounding of each rank's
 partial (switch off)

Under tensor parallelism the TileLang MoE rounded a rank's partial twice before
the cross-rank sum: the combine wrote BF16, then the runner added the shared
expert's partial in BF16. DeepSeek's reference rounds a row-parallel partial
once (RowParallelLinear: the linear's BF16 output, then an FP32 all-reduce and
one rounding).

- moe_combine_v41 and the MoE plans take an output dtype; FP32 keeps the
  routes' slot-order sum unrounded. Without a shared input the combine's unread
  Shared operand is any BF16 rows (it was the output, which an FP32 output
  cannot be).
- TileLangExperts reports its output dtype from kernels.moe_output_dtype() and
  the MoE method reports a modular kernel's experts' dtype.
- The runner adds the shared expert to a routed output wider than the layer's
  dtype in FP32 and rounds the rank's partial once before the all-reduce or
  into the reduce-scatter buffer, so the reduction stays BF16 (an FP32
  reduction measured twice the prefill reduce-scatter time on the fabric).

MOE_FP32_COMBINE is off.

(cherry picked from commit 33ef3db6abe5b91eda89d6467c42da1f5e21ef80)

